<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Estonia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Estonia is a country on the eastern shore of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baltic-sea">Baltic Sea</a>. Northern Estonia came under Swedish rule in 1561, making it one of the first Baltic provinces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-empire">Swedish Empire</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> lost it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-northern-war">Great Northern War</a>, confirmed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-nystad">Treaty of Nystad</a> in 1721.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/estonia.jpg" alt="Estonia" width="320" height="204" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Unknown author Vector: SKopp, PeepP and ‍others · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Estonia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
